    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "Find the area bounded by the line $y=2x+1$, the $y$-axis and the lines $y=3$ and $y=4$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac54=1\\dfrac14$ square units.",
      "worked": "Make $x$ the subject: $x=\\dfrac{y-1}{2}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}A&=\\int_3^4\\frac{y-1}{2}\\,dy\\\\&=\\frac12\\left[\\frac{y^2}{2}-y\\right]_3^4\\\\&=\\frac12\\left[(8-4)-\\left(\\frac92-3\\right)\\right]\\\\&=\\frac54\\\\&=1\\frac14\\text{ square units}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
